WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.760 --> 00:00:14.509
The Great Wall of China is one of the most recognizable landmarks in the world.

2
00:00:15.649 --> 00:00:17.571
It is the world's longest structure.

3
00:00:18.631 --> 00:00:22.794
In fact, some astronauts have said they could see it from space!

4
00:00:23.955 --> 00:00:31.500
Curving across the land like a sleeping dragon, it follows almost the entire northern border of China for

5
00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:33.542
more than twenty thousand kilometers.

6
00:00:34.602 --> 00:00:38.505
You might ask why a nation would need a wall along its border.

7
00:00:39.726 --> 00:00:45.630
The Chinese people built the Great Wall to protect their civilization from attacking tribes in the north.

8
00:00:46.871 --> 00:00:53.315
But the Great Wall of China took over two thousand years to complete, and during this time an

9
00:00:53.375 --> 00:00:55.696
incredible amount of history unfolded.

10
00:00:56.897 --> 00:01:05.091
The Qin dynasty was a short-lived but important dynasty because its first ruler, Emperor Qin Shi Huang, was

11
00:01:05.151 --> 00:01:06.932
a very influential emperor.

12
00:01:08.113 --> 00:01:12.676
He unified China and started the construction of the Great Wall of China.

13
00:01:13.677 --> 00:01:16.679
He used all his authority to get the wall built.

14
00:01:17.839 --> 00:01:21.122
The builders used the hang-tu method of construction.

15
00:01:22.182 --> 00:01:29.747
They erected two temporary barriers parallel to each other and packed a layer of dirt, stones, and wood

16
00:01:29.807 --> 00:01:30.408
between them.

17
00:01:31.536 --> 00:01:39.159
After many layers were built up, the temporary barriers were removed, leaving a tall, thick earthen wall.

18
00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:46.042
Watchtowers were constructed along the wall so that soldiers could see enemy armies approaching.

19
00:01:47.163 --> 00:01:53.325
If invaders attacked, the soldiers lit a fire, and the smoke was a signal to warn the soldiers

20
00:01:53.445 --> 00:01:54.806
in the other watchtowers.

21
00:01:56.006 --> 00:02:01.873
Back then there were no mechanical tools to help with construction, so all the work was done by

22
00:02:01.933 --> 00:02:10.759
hand. It was back-breaking labor, and life was very hard for the workers, especially because Emperor Qin was

23
00:02:10.879 --> 00:02:16.522
ruthless. It is believed that hundreds of thousands of men died building it.

24
00:02:17.563 --> 00:02:23.186
The Qin dynasty did not last very long after the death of Emperor Qin Shi Huang in 210

25
00:02:23.226 --> 00:02:31.436
BC. According to some accounts, he was able to build over 2,500 kilometers of the Great Wall.

26
00:02:32.637 --> 00:02:38.982
After the fall of the Qin dynasty, a leader named Liu Bang came to power and established the

27
00:02:39.042 --> 00:02:39.942
Han dynasty.

28
00:02:41.203 --> 00:02:47.888
By the time Emperor Wu Di, the seventh emperor of the Han dynasty, came to power in 141

29
00:02:47.948 --> 00:02:52.652
BC, the Great Wall had deteriorated and needed major repairs.

30
00:02:53.788 --> 00:02:57.091
Wu Di wanted to rebuild and extend the wall.

31
00:02:58.171 --> 00:03:05.516
His workers also used the hang-tu method of construction, so the architecture of the wall changed very little

32
00:03:05.917 --> 00:03:08.779
from that of the section built during the Qin dynasty.

33
00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:15.484
Wu Di's workers, however, had better working conditions, and got paid for their service.

34
00:03:16.644 --> 00:03:21.448
During Wu Di's reign, another large section of the Great Wall was completed.

35
00:03:22.620 --> 00:03:27.804
It was also during the reign of Wu Di that China started trading its riches with countries in

36
00:03:27.844 --> 00:03:28.405
the west.

37
00:03:29.546 --> 00:03:37.252
Chinese traders traveled to Central Asia, the Middle East, and even as far as Rome, bringing silk, paper,

38
00:03:37.452 --> 00:03:38.793
and spices to Europe.

39
00:03:39.914 --> 00:03:45.618
This long trading route was called the Silk Road, and the main route of the Silk Road closely

40
00:03:45.678 --> 00:03:47.560
followed the curves of the Great Wall.

41
00:03:48.848 --> 00:03:56.314
Life in villages along the wall was prosperous and peaceful during this time, but this era eventually came

42
00:03:56.394 --> 00:03:56.915
to an end.

43
00:03:58.236 --> 00:04:06.743
After the death of Emperor Wu Di in 87 BC, the Han dynasty slowly deteriorated and finally ended

44
00:04:06.823 --> 00:04:08.124
in 220 AD.

45
00:04:09.345 --> 00:04:16.051
It wasn't until a thousand years later, during the Ming dynasty, that the Great Wall became an impressive

46
00:04:16.111 --> 00:04:17.492
structure once again.

47
00:04:18.760 --> 00:04:22.921
What we see of the Great Wall today was built during the Ming dynasty.

48
00:04:24.122 --> 00:04:31.284
The first emperor and his successors maintained the Great Wall very carefully, and strengthened it to keep invaders

49
00:04:31.464 --> 00:04:36.645
out. The wall became an important project for each of the Ming emperors.

50
00:04:39.726 --> 00:04:46.208
By the time of this dynasty, new inventions had become available to help the workers with construction.

51
00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:56.403
Workers still used the hang-tu method of construction, but this time they packed the dirt and stones between

52
00:04:56.523 --> 00:04:59.745
two solid brick walls to make it more stable.

53
00:05:01.366 --> 00:05:07.508
They made the top of the wall wide enough for horse carriages to travel, and built more watchtowers.

54
00:05:08.709 --> 00:05:15.132
Now, instead of smoke signals, soldiers used gunpowder rockets to warn of an approaching enemy.

55
00:05:16.496 --> 00:05:21.099
Another improvement made to the wall during the Ming dynasty was a drainage system.

56
00:05:22.260 --> 00:05:28.263
Until then rainwater slowly collected in the wall, making it deteriorate more quickly.

57
00:05:29.464 --> 00:05:34.487
After the last Ming emperor died in 1620, construction on the wall ceased.

58
00:05:35.447 --> 00:05:36.948
The era had ended.

59
00:05:38.369 --> 00:05:45.204
For the next four centuries, China was ruled by the Qing dynasty, which did not need the wall

60
00:05:45.245 --> 00:05:46.365
to protect its borders.

61
00:05:47.625 --> 00:05:53.367
By the time the Qing dynasty collapsed and the Communist Party took control, the Great Wall was nearly

62
00:05:53.467 --> 00:06:02.669
forgotten. But in 1980 the Chinese government decided to restore the Great Wall and show it to the

63
00:06:02.729 --> 00:06:10.491
world. Today it is one of the most visited tourist attractions on earth, a silent witness to the

64
00:06:10.591 --> 00:06:15.328
many battles, wars, and changing empires of China's history.
